@niflostancu I've had a brief look at the tests, and I've identified 2 issues with the test itself:
* The init function of the fake driver used in the test did not call `ieee802154_init()` [here](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/tests/net/ieee802154/l2/src/ieee802154_fake_driver.c#L102), so the address field in the 802.15.4 context was not initialized properly,
* And the ext address configured in the [fake driver](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/tests/net/ieee802154/l2/src/ieee802154_fake_driver.c#L98) does not not match the one used in the [test frame](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/tests/net/ieee802154/l2/src/ieee802154_test.c#L206), therefore the packet is dumped an no ACK sent.
